  "_doc": "Bruno Kart's hand-picked items: the gender traps and the irregular plurals with made-up wrong plurals, and the verb gates. The lexicon adds the volume (lexWords.js). `article` is the article as the learner says it (le, la, l'), `genus` (m or f) is required with l', because l' hides the gender: those nouns are asked with un / une (questions.js, content-plan §5.9). `hAspire` marks an h aspiré (le haricot), which takes le / la. `pluralWrong` are wrong forms of the noun without article; questions.js puts les in front. A noun whose plural looks like its singular (le prix) is only asked in the plural gates. A verb has one right answer and two wrong forms; a missing `tense` means présent. `person` is the start of the sentence the form completes.",
